# Branch Finish Rules

Use this rule only when the user asks to finish a branch, open a PR, merge, or commit.

1. Verify working tree with `git status`.
2. Run the agreed verification gate, or report that it was not run.
3. Commit only when the user explicitly asks or the approved plan says to commit.
4. Stage only files in the finished slice; exclude caches and secrets.
5. Report branch name, base, commits ahead/behind, and verification results.
6. Present available finish options: keep branch, commit, push/create PR, merge locally.
7. Never force-delete branches or discard work without explicit user confirmation.
